{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeLambdaSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeLambdaSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeRotation"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_milnorWedges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_milnorWedges","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeLambdaSum.lean#L202-L229","doc":"**Milnor's Λ-sum, for the union of the three wedges.**\n\n    Vol(chimney (milnorWedges R t α β γ) R)  =  Λ(α) + Λ(β) + Λ(γ)\n\nThe hypotheses are exactly his: the three angles are positive, sum to `π`, and\nare acute.  Acuteness is used **only** through `disjoint_wedgeAt_adjacent` /\n`disjoint_wedgeAt_wrap` — a wedge fits strictly inside a half-plane bounded by\nits own edge exactly when `2ψ < π`.\n\n**This is not yet a statement about a triangle.**  `milnorWedges` is a union of\nthree explicitly-described regions of the plane.  That it EQUALS the closed\ntriangle inscribed in the circle, up to null sets, is the one remaining step —\nsee the scope note below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.milnorWedges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.milnorWedges","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeLambdaSum.lean#L195-L200","doc":"The three wedges of Milnor's subdivision, for a triangle inscribed in the\ncircle of radius `R` with inscribed angles `(α, β, γ)` and first vertex at\nangle `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_union₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_union₃","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeLambdaSum.lean#L149-L178","doc":"**The Λ-sum for three pairwise-disjoint wedges.**\n\nNothing here says the union is a triangle; the geometry lives entirely in the\ndisjointness hypotheses and in whatever supplies the three axes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.disjoint_wedgeAt_wrap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.disjoint_wedgeAt_wrap","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeLambdaSum.lean#L134-L145","doc":"The wrap-around case: `W₂`'s upper edge is `W₁`'s lower edge, one turn on.\n`2π`-periodicity of `sin`/`cos` is the only place periodicity is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.disjoint_wedgeAt_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.disjoint_wedgeAt_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeLambdaSum.lean#L118-L132","doc":"**Two wedges sharing an edge direction are disjoint.**\n\n`W₁`'s upper edge and `W₂`'s lower edge are the same line through the origin;\n`W₁` is strictly on one side of it and `W₂` strictly on the other.  No angular\narithmetic: the hypothesis `θ₁ + ψ₁ = θ₂ - ψ₂` is an equation between reals. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_lower","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeLambdaSum.lean#L95-L114","doc":"**The wedge lies strictly above its lower edge**: the line through the\norigin in direction `θ − ψ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_upper","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeLambdaSum.lean#L76-L93","doc":"**The wedge lies strictly below its upper edge**: the line through the\norigin in direction `θ + ψ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inner_perp_rotL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inner_perp_rotL","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeLambdaSum.lean#L66-L74","doc":"**Rotating, then testing against the perpendicular of the `(θ+ψ)`\ndirection, sees only `ψ`.**  The `θ` cancels — which is why the separation\nbelow is a linear inequality rather than an angular comparison. ","signatureChunk":0}]}